# Card Control API sample requests (Visual Studio: click "Send request").
# 1. Start the starter stubs and the API (see CLAUDE.md / README).
# 2. Get a token and an encrypted PAN in PowerShell from the starter folder:
#      $TOKEN = (Invoke-RestMethod -Method Post -Uri http://localhost:5090/oauth2/token -Body @{
#        grant_type='client_credentials'; client_id='partner-app'
#        client_secret='dev-only-partner-app-secret'; scope='api://card-control/.default' }).access_token
#      dotnet run tools/jwe-tool.cs -- encrypt --key .dev-keys/bank-dev-1.public.pem 4111111111111111
# 3. Paste them into the two variables below.

@CardControl.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5045
@token = PASTE_ACCESS_TOKEN
@encryptedPan = PASTE_JWE

### Lock a card
POST {{CardControl.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cards/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-1001"
}

### Unlock a card
POST {{CardControl.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cards/unlock
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-1001"
}

### Corporate not enabled (expect 403 CorporateNotEnabled)
POST {{CardControl.Api_HostAddress}}/api/cards/lock
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-Initiating-User: jane.smith@acme.example
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "encryptedPan": "{{encryptedPan}}",
  "corporateId": "CORP-3003"
}
